This patch implements a compression of backtraces:

* On a random backtrace, it will skip as many calls as necessary to reach and
  display the last 64 calls at the bottom of the stack;

* On a cyclic backtrace, it will detect cycles of size 1, 2 and 3, and
  display a message that the next entries are cycling.

Backtrace compression is enabled by default, and can be disabled by
setting the bit 1 (value 2) of the `b` parameter of
`OCAMLRUNPARAM`. Cycle detection can also be disabled independently by
setting bit 2 (value 4) of the `b` parameter.
